"""
Heritage Monitor Pipeline — Snakemake DAG.

Orchestration only: this file and rules/*.smk wire together the ordered steps.
The actual logic lives in src/sources/, src/common/, and src/enrichment/ — this file
never contains pipeline logic itself, only how to invoke it and in what order.

Rule files mirror where the code they invoke lives: rules/api_runner/ ↔
src/sources/apis/, rules/dumps.smk ↔ src/sources/dumps/, rules/external/ ↔
src/sources/external/, rules/pipeline/ ↔ pipeline-level code that isn't a source
at all (src/enrichment/, and eventually src/pipelines/core_v4/, src/pipelines/core_v3/
once it's rebuilt runnable) — each pipeline version gets its own
rules/pipeline/core_vN/ once that version has real rules, rather than
stubbing them out in advance.

Run locally:    snakemake --cores 4 <target>
Run on the HPC: snakemake --workflow-profile orchestration/profiles/slurm <target>
"""

